      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find the logic here extremely convoluted: if there\u0027s no DTBO (`overlay_buf \u003d\u003d None`), we create an empty DT (`from_overlay_onto_new_fdt(None)`) to read the properties (`get_fdt_prop_bool`) from - which obviously won\u0027t be found as it\u0027s empty - or fall back to a default value (`_ \u003d\u003e return Ok(false)` in `get_fdt_prop_bool`). And all this to obtain the same resulting constructed `DebugConfig` than if `from_custom_debug_overlay_policy` had returned `Err`, making `DebugConfig::new` use its default value (line 136) ...\n\nWhy not simply\n```suggestion\n        let overlay_buf \u003d fs::read(path)\n            .map_err(Error::msg)\n            .with_context(|| format!(\"Failed to read {path:?}\"))?;\n```\n?",
      "range": {
