      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T15:37:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you\u0027re proposing to change the behavior when the custom debug policy file is missing. Am I correct?\n\nI wrote the logic in this way to provide easy way to provide an empty debug policy in the host via `DisableMicrodroidDebugPolicyPreparer`. If you change the code here, then we need to change the preparer. Two options.\n\nOption 1) The preparer generates an empty but valid debug policy DTBO on the fly, and set its path.\n\nOption 2) Provide an empty debug policy DTBO although DTBO and preparer can\u0027t be built at once (Java vs dtc genrule). So, using the preparer requires extra setup in `AndroidTest.xml` to push the DTBO.\n\nI thought that the current code is bit better overall and easier to use it manually. What do you think?\n\n\nnot related question) How did you embed suggested edit?",
      "parentUuid": "f4b4a603_55e1a98e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 167,
