      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T09:02:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So you\u0027re proposing to change the behavior when the custom debug policy file is missing. Am I correct?\n\nNo, I\u0027m proposing to refactor the code when `CUSTOM_DEBUG_POLICY_OVERLAY_SYSPROP` is set to the path of a non-existent file (which is different from the case where no custom DP is configured) in order to remove the convoluted logic described in great detail above **without modifying the behaviour** as the suggestion keeps constructing\n```\nSelf {\n    debug_level,\n    debug_policy_log: false,\n    debug_policy_ramdump: false,\n    debug_policy_adb: false,\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "2938477e_fa7f7e4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 167,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "d8f5286c8c2c41e0b6124e3ed4ef307a2f6a2264",
