      "writtenOn": "2023-09-26T15:59:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t believe this requires any `libs/libfdt` changes as the underlying logic is straightforward:\n\n1. allocate and populate empty DT\n1. apply the overlay\n1. read the properties from their canonical `/avf/...` paths from the result\n\nnote that there\u0027s no need to backup the DTBO, like `from_overlay_onto_new_fdt` currently does, as `overlay_buf` will go out of scope and be released when we return.\n\nThe code would look something like\n```\nlet mut overlay_buf \u003d fs::read(path).map_err(...).with_context(...)?;\nlet overlay \u003d Fdt::from_mut_slice(\u0026mut overlay_buf)...?;\n\nlet mut fdt_buf \u003d vec![0_u8; fdt_estimated_size];\nlet fdt \u003d Fdt::create_empty_tree(\u0026mut fdt_buf)...?;\n\nlet fdt \u003d fdt.apply_overlay(overlay)...?; // LMK if borrow checker complains.\n\nOk(Self {\n    debug_level,\n    debug_policy_log: get_fdt_prop_bool(fdt, \u0026DP_LOG_PATH)?,\n    debug_policy_ramdump: get_fdt_prop_bool(fdt, \u0026DP_RAMDUMP_PATH)?,\n    debug_policy_adb: get_fdt_prop_bool(fdt, \u0026DP_ADB_PATH)?,\n})\n```\n\nRegarding `fdt_estimated_size`, can\u0027t we simply use `overlay.totalsize()`? Naively, I would expect the DTBO to contain all the fields that will end up in the DT and more so that `fdt.totalsize() \u003c overlay.totalsize()`; what am I missing?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "d8f5286c8c2c41e0b6124e3ed4ef307a2f6a2264",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
