      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T15:37:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re backup:\n\nBackup is to ensure that overlay remain unchanged after it\u0027s being overlaid. As you may know, overlay API amends both base and overlay while applying overlay.\n\nDo you prefer to keep it damaged? Technically we don\u0027t need to back in here and later usages, but later uses in `pvmfw` wasn\u0027t trivial to track it.\n\nUltimate solution would be refactoring `pvmfw` to move ownership of VM DTBO from `pvmfw` config payload to entries when used. With such change, I can drop VM DTBO immediately after trying overlay so backup isn\u0027t necessary. But I failed to refactor so, so wrote the API in this way. What do you think?\n\n\nRE size: you\u0027re correct. I\u0027ll fix so.",
      "parentUuid": "5a79916d_90980d56",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "d8f5286c8c2c41e0b6124e3ed4ef307a2f6a2264",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
