      "writtenOn": "2023-09-26T15:59:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alternatively to my comment above, do we have the option to not even bother to apply the DTBO and read from it directly, treating it like a regular DT? Of course, the path would differ from what we currently access but overall, it would be more efficient, if we can reliably predict what the path looks like.\n\nTo illustrate using `test_tree_overlay.dtsi`, reading `\u003cversion\u003e` of `/` in the resulting DT can be achieved by reading the property from `/node@overlay/__overlay__` in the DTBO.\n\nWDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "d8f5286c8c2c41e0b6124e3ed4ef307a2f6a2264",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
